# definitions/ — schema

One term, defined exactly once, per file (CLAUDE.md L2). `rk check`'s defs gate
(docs/gate-contracts.md Gate 1) enforces this file format; a violation is an ERROR or WARN
reported by `rk check`, not a style preference.

## Frontmatter

Flat `key: value` lines between two `---` lines, at the top of the file.

| field | required | allowed values |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | yes | must equal the filename stem (no `.md`) |
| `term` | yes | canonical human name for the concept |
| `aliases` | no | `;`-separated alternate names/symbols; folded into the same no-collision namespace as `term` |
| `kind` | yes | one of `cited`, `consensus`, `original` |
| `status` | yes | one of `draft`, `locked` |
| `source` | **required when `kind: cited`** | a source-id from `refs/manifest/SOURCES.md` (a top-level `refs/<source-id>/...` directory name); `internal` is not a special case — it is only accepted when `refs/manifest/checksums.sha256` has no entries yet (an absent/empty manifest skips this check entirely), or once it does, when `internal` is itself a registered source-id (a `refs/internal/` directory with hashed content in the manifest). Once other sources are registered, an unregistered `source: internal` is REJECTED like any other unknown source-id |
| `locus` | no | where in the source (informational only; not machine-checked) |
| `sha256` | **required when `kind: cited`** | a hex-prefix present in `refs/manifest/checksums.sha256` |
| `consensus` | **required when `kind` is `consensus` or `original`** | who agreed, or where it was transcribed |

Rules the gate enforces: `id` must match the filename stem; `term` (plus every `alias`,
case-folded) must be globally unique across every shard in this directory — two shards claiming
the same name is DRIFT, an ERROR; a `cited` shard without both `source` and `sha256` is an ERROR
(no unverifiable citations); a `status: draft` shard passes but WARNs "not yet consensus-gated".

## Example — a complete minimal shard

A file named `def-widget.md`:

```markdown
---
id: def-widget
term: widget
aliases: gadget
kind: original
status: draft
consensus: agreed in session 2026-07-18, see docs/worklog.md
---

A widget is ... (the actual definition prose goes here, after the frontmatter's closing `---`).
```

A `kind: cited` shard additionally needs `source:` and `sha256:` — e.g. replacing the last three
frontmatter lines above with:

```
kind: cited
status: draft
source: some-source-id
sha256: 0123456789abcdef
```
